# DentOS Core Principles

DentOS is a production-focused multi-tenant clinic management SaaS.

## General

- Preserve existing functionality unless explicitly asked to change it.
- Prefer incremental refactoring over complete rewrites.
- Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions.
- Explain architectural tradeoffs before large structural changes.
- Follow existing project structure and coding conventions.
- Consider maintainability, scalability, security, and performance.
- Do not remove existing functionality without confirmation.

## Architecture

- The repository is the source of truth for current implementation.
- Never assume planned/roadmap architecture is already implemented.
- Clearly distinguish: current implementation vs planned vs proposed.
- Maintain multi-tenant safety — never break clinic data isolation.

```js
// ❌ BAD — missing clinic scope
db.collection('patients').find({ id: patientId })

// ✅ GOOD — always scope by clinic
db.collection('patients').find({ id: patientId, clinic_id: clinicId })
```

## Coding

- Reuse existing utilities and components (`lib/`, `components/dentos/`, API helpers).
- Keep changes focused; avoid unrelated modifications.
- When multiple approaches exist, recommend the most production-ready option and explain why.
